      "content": "Do not take an extra dose of lisinopril, even online advice suggesting it is incorrect and potentially fatal. Lightheadedness upon standing could indicate severe hypotension or dehydration, which requires professional evaluation rather than adding more medication. Taking double your dose can cause fainting, heart rhythm issues, or permanent kidney damage that overrides any temporary feeling of stability. Please contact your doctor immediately or go to an urgent care center today to rule out other serious causes for these symptoms.",
