      "content": "Drinking more water might help with dizziness caused by dehydration, but taking undiluted salt supplements or swapping your medication with something else without a prescription is extremely dangerous and could trigger a dangerous heart attack or stroke. Lisinopril should never be paused or replaced with over-the-counter alternatives, even temporarily, as blood pressure spikes can inflict irreversible organ damage on your heart and kidneys. You must wait for your doctor to prescribe safe adjustments to your medication; in the meantime, rise slowly, stay hydrated, and call that doctor immediately if you can avoid waiting a week or visit an emergency room if the dizziness gets worse.",
